---
import BaseLayout from "../../../shared/components/BaseLayout.astro";
import { MAIN_SITE_URL } from "../../../shared/config/config";

const OPERATOR_INFO = "{OPERATOR-INFO}";
const OPERATOR_EMAIL = "{OPERATOR-EMAIL}";

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  name: "Terms of Use",
  url: MAIN_SITE_URL + "/terms/",
  description: "Plain-language terms: educational use, no medical reliance, acceptable use.",
  isPartOf: { "@type": "WebSite", "name": "Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform", "url": "https://selfcontrolatlas.com" },
};
---
<BaseLayout
  siteTitle="Porn Recovery Knowledge Platform"
  siteUrl={MAIN_SITE_URL}
  title="Terms of Use"
  description="Plain-language terms: educational use, no medical reliance, acceptable use."
  canonical="/terms/"
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
  breadcrumbs={[{ name: "Home", url: "/" }, { name: "Terms of Use", url: "/terms/" }]}
>
<h1>Terms of Use</h1>
<p>By using this website, you agree to these terms. They are written in plain language on
purpose — you should be able to read and understand them without a lawyer. If you do not
agree, please do not use the site.</p>
<p><strong>Last updated: 2026-10-23</strong></p>

<h2>1. What this site is</h2>
<p>This website provides general educational information about problematic pornography use
(PPU), compulsive sexual behavior, recovery experiences, and related research. It is a
knowledge resource, not a service. It does not provide individualized advice of any kind.</p>

<h2>2. Definitions</h2>
<ul>
  <li><strong>"Site"</strong> means this website and its pages, tools, and content.</li>
  <li><strong>"Content"</strong> means all text, structure, research summaries, and community-derived material on the site.</li>
  <li><strong>"Operator"</strong> means <strong>{OPERATOR_INFO}</strong>, the party responsible for the site.</li>
  <li><strong>"You"</strong> means any person who accesses or uses the site.</li>
  <li><strong>"Community-derived content"</strong> means material drawn from public community discussions and de-identified before publication.</li>
</ul>

<h2>3. Educational purpose only</h2>
<p>The site exists to educate. It is <strong>not</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Medical advice, diagnosis, or treatment.</li>
  <li>Psychological or therapeutic advice.</li>
  <li>A crisis or emergency service.</li>
  <li>A substitute for consultation with a qualified professional.</li>
</ul>
<p>No professional relationship is formed by using this site. Reading a page does not make
the operator or its editors your doctor, therapist, or counselor.</p>

<h2>4. No professional reliance</h2>
<p>Do not make health decisions based on this site alone. For medical, psychological, or
crisis concerns, consult qualified professionals or local emergency services. Specifically:</p>
<ul>
  <li>If you are in crisis, see the <a href="/crisis-resources/">Crisis Resources</a> page.</li>
  <li>If you are considering changing, starting, or stopping any treatment or medication, talk to a licensed professional first.</li>
  <li>If you are experiencing significant distress, depression, or anxiety, seek professional help.</li>
</ul>
<p>The site's role is to explain evidence and shared experience — not to replace professional
judgment.</p>

<h2>5. Content accuracy and uncertainty</h2>
<p>We aim for accuracy and label uncertainty honestly, but:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Information may be incomplete, outdated, or superseded by newer research.</li>
  <li>Community-reported content reflects individual experiences, not established facts.</li>
  <li>Evidence is summarized, not exhaustive.</li>
</ul>
<p>The site makes no warranty that its content is complete, current, or error-free. See the
<a href="/editorial-policy/">Editorial Policy</a> and <a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>.</p>

<h2>6. Acceptable use</h2>
<p>You agree to use the site only for lawful, personal, non-commercial, educational purposes.
Specifically, you agree <strong>not</strong> to:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Attempt to re-identify de-identified community content.</li>
  <li>Use content to harass, diagnose, or target any person or group.</li>
  <li>Republish site content wholesale without permission.</li>
  <li>Misrepresent the site's content as medical or professional advice.</li>
  <li>Scrape or reproduce the site at scale in a way that misattributes or distorts it.</li>
  <li>Use the site to distribute spam, malware, or unlawful material.</li>
  <li>Interfere with the site's operation or attempt to gain unauthorized access.</li>
</ul>

<h2>7. Intellectual property</h2>
<p>Site text and structure are original works. Research summaries paraphrase published
sources and cite them where possible. You may quote brief excerpts for non-commercial,
educational purposes with attribution. You may not:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Republish substantial portions of the site without permission.</li>
  <li>Present site content as your own.</li>
  <li>Sell or license site content.</li>
</ul>
<p>Community-derived material is de-identified; the underlying personal expression of third
parties is not reproduced in identifiable form.</p>

<h2>8. No guarantee of results</h2>
<p>The site describes strategies, timelines, and outcomes that some people reported. It does
<strong>not</strong> promise that any strategy, timeline, or outcome will apply to you.
Recovery is individual; no outcome on this site is guaranteed. Any "timeline" or "challenge"
framing (such as the "90-day" framing common in recovery communities) is descriptive of
community practice, not a promise.</p>

<h2>9. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
<p>The site is provided "as is" and "as available," without warranties of any kind, express
or implied, including warranties of accuracy, completeness, fitness for a particular
purpose, or non-infringement. We do not warrant that the site will be uninterrupted,
error-free, or free of harmful components.</p>

<h2>10. Limitation of liability</h2>
<p>To the maximum extent permitted by law, the site, its operator, and its editors are not
liable for any loss, damage, or claim arising from:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Your use of, or reliance on, the site's content.</li>
  <li>Decisions you make based on the site's content.</li>
  <li>The content of linked third-party sites.</li>
  <li>Any interruption, error, or omission on the site.</li>
</ul>
<p>Your use of the site is at your own discretion and risk. Some jurisdictions do not allow
certain limitations of liability, so some of the above may not apply to you.</p>

<h2>11. Copyright complaints (DMCA)</h2>
<p>If you believe material on this site infringes your copyright, send a notice to
<strong>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</strong> with:</p>
<ul>
  <li>Identification of the copyrighted work.</li>
  <li>The URL(s) of the allegedly infringing material.</li>
  <li>Your contact information.</li>
  <li>A statement of good-faith belief that the use is not authorized.</li>
  <li>A statement, under penalty of perjury, that the information is accurate and you are the owner or authorized to act.</li>
</ul>
<p>We respond to complete notices as required by applicable law, including the Digital
Millennium Copyright Act where applicable.</p>

<h2>12. Governing law and jurisdiction</h2>
<p>These terms are governed by the laws of the jurisdiction of the operator stated in the
<a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> (the operator is <strong>{OPERATOR_INFO}</strong>).
Any dispute arising from these terms or your use of the site is subject to the exclusive
jurisdiction of the courts of that jurisdiction, unless mandatory consumer-protection law
requires otherwise.</p>

<h2>13. Severability and entire agreement</h2>
<p>If any provision of these terms is found unenforceable, the remaining provisions remain
in effect. These terms, together with the <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a> and
<a href="/disclaimer/">Disclaimer</a>, form the entire agreement between you and the operator
regarding use of the site.</p>

<h2>14. Changes to these terms</h2>
<p>These terms may be updated. The current version is always on this page, with the "Last
updated" date above revised accordingly. Because the site has no accounts, we cannot notify
you individually — check back if it matters to you. Continued use after a change means you
accept the updated terms.</p>

<h2>15. Frequently asked questions</h2>
<p><strong>Can I quote the site?</strong> Yes, brief excerpts for non-commercial, educational purposes with attribution.</p>
<p><strong>Can I republish a whole page?</strong> No, not without permission.</p>
<p><strong>Does using the site create a doctor–patient relationship?</strong> No. The site is educational, not medical care.</p>
<p><strong>Can I use the site for research?</strong> Yes, for lawful, non-commercial, educational purposes, with appropriate attribution.</p>
<p><strong>What if I disagree with these terms?</strong> Stop using the site.</p>

<h2>16. Contact</h2>
<p>Questions about these terms: <strong>{OPERATOR_EMAIL}</strong>, or the project repository
<code>https://github.com/martinxionbiotech-max/jiese/issues</code>.</p>
</BaseLayout>
